SUMMARY:Great Scott! The Life/Work of Carol Scott — New Orleans
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270222
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:9391f1c4ad10d5e09d96fa6bbfa1@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Retrospective\,New Orleans\,United States
DESCRIPTION:A landmark solo exhibition\, “Great Scott\,” will showcase
  more than 40 of Scott’s past and current works across various media\, c
 elebrating her significant contributions to visual art in New Orleans. Mor
 eover\, it will be the first full retrospective of her work presented at a
  major New Orleans cultural institution.\nCategory: Retrospective\nOrigina
 l listing: https://www.cacno.org/programming/great-scott-a-retrospective-o
 f-the-life-work-of-carol-scott
LOCATION:Contemporary Arts Center New Orleans\, 900 Camp St\, New Orleans
 \, LA 70130
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.cacno.org/programming/great-scott-a-retrospective-of-the-l
 ife-work-of-carol-scott
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:cac-new-orleans
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nic[o] Brierre Aziz: Sweet Surrender — New Orleans
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270215
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:0d98b77a6200c5a72c9c485178d5@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Solo Exhibition\,New Orleans\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Nic[o] Brierre Aziz: "Sweet Surrender" is the Haitian-New Orle
 anian artist’s first institutional solo exhibition\, and surveys a range
  of works in performance\, photography\, sculpture\, and installation crea
 ted over the last ten years. Whether turning to Southern antebellum histor
 y or contemporary art markets\, Aziz’s work interrogates the de/valuatio
 n of Black life and cultural heritage\, both exposing and subverting syste
 ms of cultural\, political\, and economic power.\nCategory: Solo Exhibitio
 n\nOriginal listing: https://www.cacno.org/programming/sugar
LOCATION:Contemporary Arts Center New Orleans\, 900 Camp St\, New Orleans
 \, LA 70130
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.cacno.org/programming/sugar
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:cac-new-orleans
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Filmed @ Hambidge 2026 Premiere — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T150000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:3c57ba5a953eee22798e2fa6e313@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Hambidge is set to premiere the fourth year of FILMED @ Hambid
 ge\, a collaborative project pairing filmmakers with artists across discip
 lines to capture the creative process on film. A signature element of the 
 program is the “meta film\,” in which an additional filmmaker turns th
 e lens on the filmmakers themselves\, documenting their creative processes
  as they interpret the work of Hambidge artists. The 2026 featured pairing
 s include Paras Chaudhari\, filming Simone Baron\; John Dierre\, filming S
 ummer Blanco and Jordan Argrett\; Ebony Blanding\, filming Michi Meko\; an
 d Priscila Torres\, filming Coulter Fussell. Lev Omelchenkov will create t
 his year’s meta film\, documenting the filmmakers and the col\nCategory:
  Film + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/filmed-hambidg
 e-2026-premiere/
LOCATION:The Tara Theatre\, 2345 Cheshire Bridge Road N.E.\, Atlanta\, GA
 \, 30324
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/filmed-hambidge-2026-premiere/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Liv’s Last Ride Screening with Director Q&A — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T130000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T150000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:6a78498ea598d80859c9db04ea0b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Liv’s Last Ride (2026) is an independent horror-comedy slash
 er film written and directed by Thaddeus Armstrong. When an unexpected vis
 itor disrupts a secluded bachelorette party\, a group of former friends mu
 st confront their shared dark history in order to survive the night. The e
 vent (part of the Buried Alive Film Festival) includes a Q&A with the film
 ’s director.\nCategory: Film + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl
 .org/event/livs-last-ride-screening-with-director-qa/
LOCATION:The Plaza Theatre\, 1049 Ponce de Leon Ave.\, Atlanta\, 30306
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/livs-last-ride-screening-with-director-q
 a/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A FINE LINE — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T200000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:6ad906c561669c9f9718dfd76bad@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Spalding Nix Fine Art is pleased to announce A FINE LINE\, a p
 resentation of four shows by Kate Hooray Osmond\, Nancy Talero\, Shannon D
 avis and Laura Dargan on view January 24 – March 20. Charleston-based in
 terdisciplinary Artist Kate Hooray Osmond’s “Americana” explores her
  evolving relationship with the shifting landscape of America through vibr
 ant and expressive genre scene paintings. Atlanta-based Artist Nancy Taler
 o’s “Super Nature” is a series of geometric modular paintings explor
 ing the merging and blurred boundaries of the natural and supernatural wor
 lds. Atlanta-based multi-media Artist Shannon Davis’s “Conversations i
 n Motion” is a series of photographic digital compositions explorin\nCat
 egory: Art + Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-fin
 e-line/2026-11-08/
LOCATION:Spalding Nix Fine Art\, 425 Peachtree Hills Ave NE Suite 30A\, At
 lanta\, GA\, 30305
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/a-fine-line/2026-11-08/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Duruflé REQUIEM — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261108T200000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:872e108003e743234b649a09039b@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Adult Choir and Schola of St. Luke’s Episcopal Church pr
 esent Maurice Duruflé’s masterpiece in a concert setting\, conducted by
  William Fred Scott. The concert will be preceded by a 6 p.m. lecture on t
 he work by Ned Tipton\, renowned student of the late Marie-Madeleine Duruf
 lé and noted authority on the music of Maurice Duruflé. The concert feat
 ures New York based mezzo-soprano Tami Petty and cellist Guang Wang\, acco
 mpanied in the solo organ version by organists Matthew Michael Brown and J
 onathan Easter.\nCategory: Music\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.or
 g/event/durufle-requiem/
LOCATION:St. Luke’s Episcopal Church\, 435 Peachtree St. NE\, Atlanta\, 
 GA\, 30308
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/durufle-requiem/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:illumine 2026 — Atlanta
