SUMMARY:Jazz at All Saints’ Presents Kenny Banks Jr. — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261113T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261113T203000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:316e7e69c8c72d708e924c172ff1@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Music\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Atlanta’s own Kenny Banks Jr.\, a Yamaha artist\, has earned
  a reputation as one of the most dynamic jazz artists in the Southeast and
  headlines the November 13 concert. Noted for his distinctive technique of
  blending jazz and gospel styles\, Banks’s repertoire also includes flav
 ors of Afro-Cuban and hip-hop sounds gathered from performing and recordin
 g around the world with a variety of artists. A brilliant solo artist\, Ba
 nks is also a regular on tour with vocalist Kurt Elling and vibraphonist S
 tefon Harris. He began playing the piano at age seven\, and in his trainin
 g with his father\, Kenny Banks Sr.\, also a pianist\, he learned the fund
 amentals of music theory\, jazz\, and composition. Under the\nCategory: Mu
 sic\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/jazz-at-all-saints-pr
 esents-kenny-banks-jr-november-13-2026-700pm/
LOCATION:All Saints&#8217\; Episcopal Church &#8211\; Atlanta\, 634 West P
 eachtree Street Northwest\, Atlanta\, 30308
