 look at human values of Harvest\, Family\, Feast and Home through a modern
  midtown Atlanta perspective\, and in the process we discover those things
  we are most grateful for. On the occasion of our country’s 250th birthd
 ay\, we recognize that our viewpoint is shaped by the paths that brought u
 s here\, so we sing of Our American Journeys. Our musical journey begins w
 ith the indigenous people on whose land we gather. We sing songs of the co
 lonial years from William Billings\, the first American-bor\nCategory: Mus
