SUMMARY:National Buy Nothing Day at the Center — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261128T120000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261128T160000
DTSTAMP:20261109T064209Z
UID:3f1266c53aa0113793268e1f3883@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Books\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The day after Thanksgiving is often known as one of the bigges
 t shopping days of the year\, but National Buy Nothing Day invites us to p
 ause and think differently about consumption\, community\, and the impact 
 of our choices. Join the Center for an afternoon of learning and reflectio
 n as we explore how everyday purchasing decisions affect people\, communit
 ies\, and the environment. Through engaging activities and conversations\,
  visitors will gain new perspectives on ethical consumption and discover w
 ays to make more intentional choices.\nCategory: Books\nOriginal listing: 
 https://www.artsatl.org/event/national-buy-nothing-day-at-the-center/
LOCATION:National Center for Civil and Human Rights\, 100 Ivan Allen Jr. B
 oulevard NW\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30313
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/national-buy-nothing-day-at-the-center/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
